<http://data.silknow.org/object/82c4601f-ec82-3e64-b0ba-e3d549a749fb>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Sash of silk and gold thread, Baluchistan, 19th century"@en , "Sash of silk decorated with bands in red, grey, yellow and green silk and gold thread. At each end of the sash are four narrower stripes of each colour and a gold band 28.5 inches long. Black silk warp, tabby woven. In the bands of gold, the wefts of gold thread are carried across 6 warp threads at once. At each end is a fringe about 2.5 inches long formed by the black warp threads together with a short tuft of gold thread. The gold thread is a gilt metal strip on a silk core. The selvages are oversewn with gold thread."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/c75eca3e-9abd-3f35-85e9-16b39557db0f> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Sash of silk decorated with bands in red, grey, yellow and green silk and gold thread. At each end of the sash are four narrower stripes of each colour and a gold band 28.5 inches long. Black silk warp, tabby woven. In the bands of gold, the wefts of gold thread are carried across 6 warp threads at once. At each end is a fringe about 2.5 inches long formed by the black warp threads together with a short tuft of gold thread. The gold thread is a gilt metal strip on a silk core. The selvages are oversewn with gold thread."@en , "Sash of silk and gold thread, Baluchistan, 19th century"@en ;
